# inc-5v5l: Dispel Evil follows the SRD -- one touch per casting, and the
# touch ends the whole spell.
#
# THE RULE. lib/pspells.irh's "Dispel Evil" has two components:
#   component 0  xval TRAP_EVENT, yval EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE) -- the +4 (+6 vs
#                inherently evil) deflection bonus, which fires only while
#                the caster is the victim of a strike.
#   component 1  aval AR_TOUCH, lval -- one touch per casting, and when that
#                touch lands on an evil creature the banish or the +10
#                dispel-magic branch runs and the WHOLE spell must end: the
#                deflection stati and the remaining TOUCH_ATTACK must both go.
#
# THE SCENE. The setup (dispel-evil-touch-setup.keys) builds an orc priest of
# Aiswin raised to character level 11 through Free Advancement and learns
# Dispel Evil through Learn Any Spell (innate -> caster level 11). Freeze
# Monsters keeps everything still.
#
# A goblin is summoned TWO squares east: out of melee reach, so nothing can
# be touched at cast time. Dispel Evil's touch component carries no qval, so
# casting opens no targeting prompt -- the same shape Minor Drain's phase-6
# check relies on (tools/keys/minor-drain-touch.keys). The script then closes
# the gap and bump-attacks once per dump until a touch lands. A touch swing
# can miss (it rolls against the goblin's touch defence); a miss is retried.
# The goblin is evil (MA_EVIL) and is not an outsider, so the landed touch
# takes the dispel-magic branch, not the banish branch.
#
# THE ORACLE is the DISPEL_EVIL_PROBE build (src/Fight.cpp), which logs at
# the landed-touch path, before and after EV_MAGIC_STRIKE:
#   "before effect=Dispel Evil touch=<mag>/<present> defl=<0|1> evil=<0|1>"
#   "after  effect=Dispel Evil touch=<mag>/<present> defl=<0|1> evil=<0|1>"
# tools/check_dispel_evil.sh asserts one "before" with touch magnitude 1, and
# that the "after" line has touch 0/0 and defl 0 -- nothing of the spell left.

@include dispel-evil-touch-setup.keys

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT RIGHT ENTER
@dump:before-cast

m
@choose "Dispel Evil"
@dump:after-cast

RIGHT
@dump:closed-distance
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-1
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-2
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-3
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-4
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-5
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-6
@dump:messages
@quit
